","s3","s4","s5"],"monitor_id":"candidate:e-1856f1a4de6f33a1e989bc09","relation":{"from":"Stirring","relation":"prevents","to":"sticking"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]},{"context":"general","correspondence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"],"evidence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"],"monitor_id":"candidate:e-634748bf2004b5616d4885b1","relation":{"from":"Stirring","relation":"prevents","to":"mushiness"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]},{"context":"general","correspondence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"],"evidence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"],"monitor_id":"candidate:e-671a0b9c4e910f5aaaf2f4c0","relation":{"from":"jasmine rice","relation":"related","to":"delicate"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]},{"context":"general","correspondence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"],"evidence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"],"monitor_id":"candidate:e-b7c1ef7263088eec592e4ae5","relation":{"from":"Rule","relation":"prevents","to":"sticking"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]},{"context":"general","correspondence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"],"evidence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"],"monitor_id":"candidate:e-e3ed4f998ffe729bf6d02b7d","relation":{"from":"jasmine rice","relation":"causes","to":"mushiness"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]},{"context":"general","correspondence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"],"evidence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"],"monitor_id":"candidate:e-fb91aba0bc594e0eb2ade0e6","relation":{"from":"Rule","relation":"prevents","to":"mushiness"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]}],"prompt_version":"p2-assessor-production-v9","replay_ancestry":[{"root":"97d5f609-c3cf-42cd-b90b-516cfef64369","source_slot":"s0"},{"root":"72ce9d5e-a9f7-4c12-b48c-2ed9e3459072","source_slot":"s1"},{"root":"606639e5-9703-425f-b860-83de31294169","source_slot":"s2"},{"root":"23a33ceb-2b93-49b7-bfa5-d0a9252cc004","source_slot":"s3"}],"schema_version":"p2-assessor-v6","source_purpose_mask":["external_evidence","model_output"],"sources":[{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s0","source_id":"97d5f609-c3cf-42cd-b90b-516cfef64369","text":"I think I'll go with the stew style. But just to be safe, should I cook the rice separately first?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s1","source_id":"72ce9d5e-a9f7-4c12-b48c-2ed9e3459072","text":"No need to cook the rice separately! You can simply add your rice and let it simmer right along with the chicken and beans in the same pot. The simmering process will cook the rice perfectly to match the timing of the stew!\n\nFor a \"stew\" style, here’s how I recommend adjusting the timing:\n\n1.  **Start with the Chicken and Beans:** Bring your broth to a boil first, then add your chicken and the beans to let those simmer and get the flavors to meld.\n2.  **The Rice Addition:** Once you've got that simmering, add your rice into the pot. \n3.  **Simmer and Wait:** Let everything simmer together until the rice is cooked through and the sauce has thickened nicely.\n\nLet me know if you want to add any specific seasonings to make the flavor profile even more interesting!"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s2","source_id":"606639e5-9703-425f-b860-83de31294169","text":"That’s reassuring. I was worried about the rice turning out too mushy, but I guess the timing will take care of that. Do you think I should adjust the liquid amount if I’m cooking everything together?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s3","source_id":"23a33ceb-2b93-49b7-bfa5-d0a9252cc004","text":"That's a great question! Since you are cooking the rice right along with the rest of the stew, yes, you should definitely adjust the liquid!\n\nThe general rule of thumb for rice is that **1 part rice to 1.5 or 2 parts liquid** (depending on how thirsty your rice is).\n\nSince you're doing a stew, I'd suggest starting with a **1:2 ratio of liquid to rice**. For example, if you are using 1 cup of rice, start with about 2 cups of broth or water. If you use more than that, it might end up mushy!\n\nIf you're worried about it getting too soft, you might need to reduce the liquid slightly, especially if you're using **long-grain rice**, as that tends to soak up less water!\n\nDo you have a specific type of rice you're using? Knowing the type can help me give you a more precise ratio!"},{"available":true,"role":"external","slot":"s4","source_id":"1ea97863-fc04-43f1-9bab-07ecc789aacc","text":"I think I'll go with the 1:2 ratio for now, but I'll keep an eye on it. I'm using jasmine rice, which I've heard is a bit more delicate. Do you think that changes anything?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s5","source_id":"81c009a4-0bae-4dee-ab59-0a98b0bd6a64","text":"That's a good point! Since jasmine rice is often a bit more \"delicate\" than longer-grain rice, it can sometimes be more sensitive to overcooking or being slightly too wet.\n\nIf you're concerned about the rice turning mushy, here are a couple of tips for that \"delicate\" rice:\n\n1.  **Reduce the initial liquid:** Since jasmine rice absorbs a lot of liquid, you might actually need slightly less than the 1:2 ratio if your liquid is very watery. I'd suggest starting with a **1:1.5 ratio of liquid to rice** and then checking the texture after the first 20 minutes.\n2.  **The \"Stirring\" Rule:** To prevent sticking or mushiness, make sure to stir it *very* gently once you've started simmering, and check the consistency after the initial boil.\n\nFor jasmine rice, I'd recommend starting with the slightly lower 1:1.5 or even 1:1 ratio to be extra safe against mushiness!\n\nLet me know how it turns out! Are you making a specific type of stew, or is this just a general cooking project?"}]},"resolved":[{"provenance":{"ancestry":[],"applicable_categories":["no_identified_link"],"corresponding_source_slots":["s5"],"credit_eligible":true,"dependence":"no_identified_link","monitor_id":"candidate:e-1856f1a4de6f33a1e989bc09","provenance_group_keys":[],"resolution_reason":"runtime_source_role_and_recorded_ancestry","schema_version":"p2-provenance-v1"},"semantic":{"corresponding_source_slots":["s5"],"coverage":{"complete":true,"reason":null,"source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]},"evidence":{"end":741,"quote":"**The \"Stirring\" Rule:** To prevent sticking or mushiness, make sure to stir it *very* gently once you've started simmering, and check the consistency after the initial boil.","source_slot":"s5","start":567},"expression_status":"affirmed","monitor_id":"candidate:e-1856f1a4de6f33a1e989bc09","relation_support":"supported","status":"present"}},{"provenance":{"ancestry":[],"applicable_categories":["no_identified_link"],"corresponding_source_slots":["s5"],"credit_eligible":true,"dependence":"no_identified_link","monitor_id":"candidate:e-634748bf2004b5616d4885b1","provenance_group_keys":[],"resolution_reason":"runtime_source_role_and_recorded_ancestry","schema_version":"p2-provenance-v1"},"semantic":{"corresponding_source_slots":["s5"],"coverage":{"complete":true,"reason":null,"source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]},"evidence":{"end":741,"quote":"**The \"Stirring\" Rule:** To prevent sticking or mushiness, make sure to stir it *very* gently once you've started simmering, and check the consistency after the initial boil.","source_slot":"s5","start":567},"expression_status":"affirmed","monitor_id":"candidate:e-634748bf2004b5616d4885b1","relation_support":"supported","status":"present"}},{"provenance":{"ancestry":[],"applicable_categories":["no_identified_link"],"corresponding_source_slots":["s5"],"credit_eligible":false,"dependence":"no_identified_link","monitor_id":"candidate:e-671a0b9c4e910f5aaaf2f4c0","provenance_group_keys":[],"resolution_reason":"runtime_source_role_and_recorded_ancestry","schema_versi